{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>When a fire goes out.</b> Even on its own (Bava Kamma 22)." "<b>And finds thorns.</b> קרדו\"נש בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>And consumes the stack.</b> It fed along the thorns until it reached the stack or the standing grain connected to the ground." "<b>Or the field.</b> It consumed its plowed furrow, and one must plow it a second time (Bava Kamma 60)." "<b>He who set the fire shall make full restitution.</b> Even though he kindled within his own property, and it went out on its own by way of thorns it found — he is liable to pay, because he did not guard his coal so that it would not go out and cause damage."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French cardons, 'thistles/thorns'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:48.964655925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}